   Peak droop without ringing = Q/C: to keep it <= 50 mV (so logic and comparator stay functional, ESTIMATE) the on-chip decap must be C >= Q/50 mV:  simultaneous 2.17 nF, staggered 0.72 nF.
   MOS gate decap density ~4.6 fF/um2 (ESTIMATE, see code comment): 2.17 nF = 0.47 mm2 (simultaneous), 0.72 nF = 0.16 mm2 (staggered).  Slot ~1.23 mm2; ADCs themselves 0.136 mm2.  MIM decap (2 fF/um2) is ~2.3x worse per area unless overlaid on circuits.
   => the supply is the biggest ADC risk of this architecture; staggering divides the peak charge (and the decap area) by ~3.0 for 7 flops and 7 extra clocks.  The ring-down needs R >~ 0.2-0.5 ohm of series damping (not known): D2/D4 simulate with an L-C-R supply model (Decision 27).

== 4. Area (ESTIMATE; D0 per-ADC cell numbers, PLAN.md section 2: DAC 9,400 + comparator 2,000 + SAR logic 25 flops x 75 + 80 gates x 15 + switches/drivers 1,500)
   per ADC: DAC 9400 + comparator 2000 + SAR logic 3075 + switches 1500 + 12 chain mux2 x 25 um2 = 300  = 16275 um2
   shared digital (frame counter 8 + ID counter 3 + stagger token chain 7 + config shift 9 + config hold 9 + control 3 = 39 flops x 75, ~150 gates x 15, + 1,000 clock/buffers) = 6175 um2
   8 ADCs 130200 um2 + shared 6175 = 136375 um2 = 0.136 mm2   (TAPEOUT.md estimate ~0.13 mm2: confirmed).  Decap is NOT included: 0.16 mm2 (staggered) to 0.47 mm2 (simultaneous) of MOS decap if the 50 mV peak criterion is kept (section 3).
   alternatives not chosen: 96 separate capture flops + 96 load/shift mux2 = ~9600 um2 extra (vs 2400 for reusing the SAR result registers as the chain); ID-less 96-bit stream saves 3 flops, but breaks the Decision 18 word.

== 5. Power (ESTIMATE) at 8 x 4 kS/s = 32 kS/s total, 3.3 V
   DAC switching 233 pJ x 32 kS/s = 7.4 uW;  comparator + SAR logic (D0 formula) 0.67 uW;  readout chain 128 clocks x 96 flops x 0.2 pJ x 4 kHz = 9.8 uW;  clock tree 1.5 pF x 160 clocks x 4 kHz = 10.5 uW
   total ADC + interface 28 uW (8.6 uA at 3.3 V) = 1.4 % of the 8 amplifiers (8 x 245 uW = 1.96 mW, SIMULATED A4a typical); the digital readout and the clock tree, not the DAC, dominate (D0 assumed ~17 uW).

== 6. Acquisition: reset to 1.65 V or not (ESTIMATE + SIMULATED A4b data)
   f_SCLK 1.0 MHz: ADC i reconnects to its amplifier 19.0 us after the sample instant; the output moves at most 942 V/s x that = 17.9 mV = 22.2 LSB, plus the code residual (<= ~2 LSB, D1/D2) -> step at reconnect ~19.5 mV
   f_SCLK 3.5 MHz: ADC i reconnects to its amplifier 5.4 us after the sample instant; the output moves at most 942 V/s x that = 5.1 mV = 6.4 LSB, plus the code residual (<= ~2 LSB, D1/D2) -> step at reconnect ~6.7 mV
   f_SCLK 5.0 MHz: ADC i reconnects to its amplifier 3.8 us after the sample instant; the output moves at most 942 V/s x that = 3.6 mV = 4.4 LSB, plus the code residual (<= ~2 LSB, D1/D2) -> step at reconnect ~5.2 mV
   A4b SIMULATED (sim/a4b_adc245.log, no reset, C_s 17 pF behind 1 kOhm, step +-0.24 V = the sample-to-sample step of a 300 Hz full-scale sine): |err| at 245 us <= 0.26 LSB (0.21 uV input-referred) typ/ff 85/ss -40; <= 0.48 LSB even at 11 us.
   The reconnect step is ~47x smaller than the 0.24 V tested, so the A4b run is a conservative bound (error scales ~linearly with the step: ESTIMATE <= 0.006 LSB).
   Reset to 1.65 V (A4b SIMULATED, sim/a4b_adc.log): -0.74..-2.25 LSB at 11 us and 0.4-2 mV left 240 us later; needs one more switch per ADC and a 1.65 V source -> REJECTED (also in Decision 28).
   Large steps (power-up: C_s at 0 V, or an artifact): worst-corner follower sink 3.26 uA, tau 315 ns (D0, SIMULATED A4a): 1.65 V down = 11.2 us to 0.5 LSB, well inside T_ACQ; the stage-2 loop kick (error ~ step^2, A4b) is ESTIMATED at (1.65/0.5)^2 x (0.4-2 mV) = 4-22 mV at 240 us for a 1.65 V step, decaying with the 0.3-0.5 ms loop constant -> discard the first ~10 frames (2.5 ms) after reset.

